import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="about · FloodWatch.PH" pathname="/me" description="About FloodWatch.PH: open-source observed flood extent from Sentinel-1 SAR, built by Xavier Puspus.">
  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-12">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-500 mb-3 font-mono">about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl mb-5 leading-tight">FloodWatch.PH</h1>

    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      FloodWatch.PH is an open-source project measuring observed flood extent during Philippine typhoons from Sentinel-1 C-band SAR satellite data, and identifying communities that are modeled flood-prone yet under-observed in the historical record.
    </p>

    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
      Built by <strong>Xavier Puspus</strong>. The same playbook as <a href="https://solar-map-ph.org" class="text-accent-steel no-underline">SolarMap.PH</a>: 100% public-licensed inputs, reproducible pipeline, bit-exact model hash, two separate tracks with two separate metrics reported honestly.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl mt-8 mb-3">The two-track architecture</h2>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      <strong>Track A</strong> is the event track: Sentinel-1 SAR flood extent for a specific typhoon, per acquisition date. Validated against GFD event 4300 (Koppu 2015). Applied to the ungauged Carina 2024 demo event. Parameter-free (Otsu threshold); no train/test leakage possible.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      <strong>Track B</strong> is the recurrence model: Google AlphaEarth 64-dim satellite embeddings (2017 annual) plus a logistic regression head trained on 57 GFD Philippines events. Event-disjoint holdout: entire typhoon events held out, never random pixels. Platt-calibrated. Hash-verified.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-xl mt-8 mb-3">Civic thesis</h2>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      Philippine communities flood repeatedly, yet the historical observed record is uneven. FloodWatch.PH measures the v1.0 gap: provinces the recurrence model flags as flood-prone but that appear with few or no events in the historical observed record (Global Flood Database). Exposure and the modeled-vs-observed gap are aggregated to province (FAO GAUL level-2, ~82 Philippine provinces); city and barangay resolution is a v1.1 refinement. The cross-reference against the official UP NOAH / PAGASA / MGB hazard maps is also v1.1, deferred because those government layers are token-gated or SPA-only.
    </p>
    <p class="text-base text-ink-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">
      Super Typhoon Carina (Gaemi) July 2024 had no promptly-public official flood-extent polygon. That absence is the civic vacuum the demo fills.
    </p>

